# G9POS — Data Model Rules

## ID Convention
All IDs are UUIDs generated on the device. Never use auto-increment integers.
```dart
// Flutter — generate on device
import 'package:uuid/uuid.dart';
final id = const Uuid().v4();
```
```go
// Go — use google/uuid
import "github.com/google/uuid"
id := uuid.New().String()
```

## Every Sync Table Has These Columns
```
id          TEXT/UUID     Primary key — UUID, device-generated
created_at  INTEGER/TIMESTAMPTZ  Unix ms (SQLite) / TIMESTAMPTZ (PostgreSQL)
updated_at  INTEGER/TIMESTAMPTZ
deleted_at  INTEGER/TIMESTAMPTZ  NULL = active, non-null = soft deleted
device_id   TEXT/UUID     Device that last modified this record
```
Exception: `inventory_events` — append-only, has no `updated_at` or `deleted_at`.

## Soft Delete — Always
```dart
// ✅ Correct — soft delete
Future<void> softDelete(String id) =>
  (update(table)..where((t) => t.id.equals(id)))
    .write(TableCompanion(
      deletedAt: Value(DateTime.now().millisecondsSinceEpoch)
    ));

// ❌ Wrong — never hard delete
await (delete(table)..where((t) => t.id.equals(id))).go();
```

Always filter soft-deleted records in every read query:
```dart
// ✅ Always include this filter
..where((t) => t.deletedAt.isNull())
```

## Inventory Events — Append Only
`inventory_events` is the most important table. Rules:
- **Never UPDATE or DELETE rows in this table**
- **Never store computed stock** — always `SUM(quantity_delta)`
- `quantity_delta` is signed: negative = stock out, positive = stock in
- Every row has a `reference_id` linking it to its parent (sale, order) — except standalone events

**Standalone events** (`INVENTORY_ADJUSTED`, `INVENTORY_DAMAGED`, `INVENTORY_RETURNED`) have `reference_id = NULL` — they have no parent entity.

**Local stock query (SQLite) — must exclude rejected events:**
```dart
// ✅ Correct — excludes rejected
final stock = await (selectOnly(inventoryEvents)
  ..addColumns([inventoryEvents.quantityDelta.sum()])
  ..where(inventoryEvents.productId.equals(productId))
  ..where(inventoryEvents.rejectedAt.isNull()))  // ← required
  .getSingle();
```

**Server stock query (PostgreSQL) — unchanged, no rejected_at:**
```sql
SELECT SUM(quantity_delta) FROM inventory_events WHERE product_id = $1;
```

## G1 — rejected_at Column (SQLite only)
`inventory_events` has a SQLite-only column `rejected_at INTEGER NULL`.

**Invariant:** `rejected_at IS NOT NULL → synced_at IS NULL`
- Only set on rows the server never saw
- Never sent to server, never replicated
- Enforced in repository layer AND as a SQLite CHECK constraint

```dart
// ✅ Marking rejection — enforce invariant
Future<void> markRejected(String eventId) async {
  final event = await getById(eventId);
  if (event.syncedAt != null) {
    throw StateError('Cannot reject a synced event: $eventId');
  }
  await (update(inventoryEvents)..where((e) => e.id.equals(eventId)))
    .write(InventoryEventsCompanion(
      rejectedAt: Value(DateTime.now().millisecondsSinceEpoch)
    ));
}
```

## SQLite vs PostgreSQL Differences
| Concern | SQLite (Drift) | PostgreSQL |
|---------|---------------|------------|
| Timestamps | INTEGER (Unix ms) | TIMESTAMPTZ |
| Booleans | INTEGER (0/1) | BOOLEAN |
| UUIDs | TEXT | UUID native |
| Extra columns | `synced_at`, `rejected_at` (inventory_events only) | `server_received_at` |
| sync_queue | Present | Not present |
| devices table | Not present | Present |

## Price and Currency
All prices stored as integers (Myanmar Kyat, no decimals):
```dart
// ✅ Correct
final priceMmk = 13000; // integer

// ❌ Wrong
final price = 130.00; // no decimals in MMK
```

## Timestamps
All timestamps are Unix milliseconds in SQLite:
```dart
// ✅ Correct
final now = DateTime.now().millisecondsSinceEpoch; // int

// ❌ Wrong — never store DateTime objects in Drift
```

## Migrations
- Never modify an existing migration file
- Every `up` migration has a `down` migration
- Format: `{sequence}_{description}.{direction}.sql`
- Migrations run automatically on server startup
